#![deny(missing_docs)]
//! Envelope encryption for secrets kept in Postgres.
//!
//! One data key per scope (an account, a sign-in attempt), generated by KMS
//! once ([`kms::EnvelopeKms::generate_data_key`]) and stored only wrapped
//! under an encryption context that names its purpose and owner, so KMS
//! refuses to unwrap it anywhere else. Values are sealed locally with
//! AES-256-GCM under the plaintext key ([`cipher::ValueCipher`]), with
//! associated data binding each ciphertext to its scope and the caller's
//! labels.
//!
//! The plaintext key lives only in memory ([`cipher::DataKey`]: zeroized on
//! drop, redacted in `Debug`, not serializable). A database dump alone
//! decrypts nothing; every unwrap is an IAM-gated, CloudTrail-recorded KMS
//! call. Use one KMS key per feature: whatever can unwrap its data keys can
//! read every scope sealed under it.

